---1463811839-914693253-1032433186=:18297
Content-Type: TEXT/PLAIN; CHARSET=US-ASCII
Content-ID: <Pine.LNX.4.44L.0209190359591.18297@hunger.screamingdaemon.com>

On Thu, 19 Sep 2002, Harald Welte wrote:

> a) it is not conforming the system all other patches use
> b) if I apply the patch to the iptables subdirectory, and somebody
>    has an old (unpatched) kernel source installed, compilation will fail.
>    This is what we usually solve with the '.*-test' files in the extensions
>    directory.
>

alright, I hope I did everything okay, attached is a tar-ball with all
the patch-o-matic files and a proper patch to iptables tar-ball with the
.*-test file.

This version allows u_int64_t counter values and allows the user to
specify values in (K)ilobit, (M)egabit, (G)igabit. It will also display
values in (K)ilobit, (M)egabit, (G)igabit when an iptables -L is performed
but saves the values out in their full u_int64_t value.

ctvolume v1.2.7a options:
   --packet-{lt,gt,eq} num     match by 'num' packets in one direction.
   --byte-{lt,gt,eq}   num     match by 'num' bytes in one direction

                               'num' allows 'KMG' suffixes to signify
                               units of (K)ilobit, (M)egabit, (G)igabit.

Let me know if anything is missing, etc.

Thanks,
jay-s.

